---@alias gcp.healthcare_v1.FhirStoreVersionEnum "VERSION_UNSPECIFIED"|"DSTU2"|"STU3"|"R4"|"R5"

---A (sub) field of a type.
---@class gcp.healthcare_v1.Field
---@field name? string The name of the field. For example, "PID-1" or just "1".
---@field minOccurs? number The minimum number of times this field must be present/repeated.
---@field maxOccurs? number The maximum number of times this field can be repeated. 0 or -1 means unbounded.
---@field type? string The type of this field. A Type with this name must be defined in an Hl7TypesConfig.
---@field table? string The HL7v2 table this field refers to. For example, PID-15 (Patient's Primary Language) usually refers to table "0296".

---@alias gcp.healthcare_v1.FieldList gcp.healthcare_v1.Field[]

---Specifies FHIR paths to match, and how to handle de-identification of matching fields.
---@class gcp.healthcare_v1.FieldMetadata
---@field action? gcp.healthcare_v1.FieldMetadataActionEnum|string Optional. Deidentify action for one field.
---@field paths? gcp.healthcare_v1.StringList Optional. List of paths to FHIR fields to be redacted. Each path is a period-separated list where each component is either a field name or FHIR type name, for example: Patient, HumanName. For "choice" types (those defined in the FHIR spec with the form: field[x]) we use two separate components. For example, "deceasedAge.unit" is matched by "Deceased.Age.unit". Supported types are: AdministrativeGenderCode, Base64Binary, Boolean, Code, Date, DateTime, Decimal, HumanName, Id, Instant, Integer, LanguageCode, Markdown, Oid, PositiveInt, String, UnsignedInt, Uri, Uuid, Xhtml.

---@alias gcp.healthcare_v1.FieldMetadataActionEnum "ACTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"TRANSFORM"|"INSPECT_AND_TRANSFORM"|"DO_NOT_TRANSFORM"

---@alias gcp.healthcare_v1.FieldMetadataList gcp.healthcare_v1.FieldMetadata[]

